{"results":[{"url":"https://rollcalltrack.com/","final_url":"https://rollcalltrack.com/","title":"Roll Call Track: Congress Votes, Bills & Stock Trades","description":"Nonpartisan tracker of U.S. Congress roll-call votes, bills, members and STOCK Act stock trades, from official House, Senate and Clerk records.","language":"en","text":"Heads up: Senate financial disclosures have not updated since Oct 23, 2026. We're working on it; other data on this page is current as shown below.\n\nData updated: Senate votes through Sep 29, 2026 · House votes through Sep 16, 2026 · House disclosures synced Nov 2, 2026 · Senate disclosures synced Oct 23, 2026. Sources\n\n# Roll Call Track: Congress votes, bills and stock trades\n\nRoll Call Track is an independent, nonpartisan tracker of the United States Congress. We follow every recorded roll-call vote in the House and Senate, the bills and nominations those votes decide, and the stock trades members of Congress disclose under the STOCK Act. Vote tallies come from the official House Clerk and Senate records, and trades come from the periodic transaction reports members file with the House Clerk and the Senate's electronic disclosure system. We publish the record as filed and do not endorse any party, candidate or position.\n\nUse the sections below to see how your senators and representative voted, read the latest roll calls, check what bills are moving, and review recent financial disclosures. Each vote page lists every member's position and a party-by-party breakdown, and each member page shows their recent votes and reported trades.\n\n## Latest Senate votes\n\n* Senate roll call 256: Keith Sonderling, of Florida, to be Secretary of Labor (PN1129) — Nomination Confirmed, Sep 30, 2026\n* Senate roll call 255: Keith Sonderling, of Florida, to be Secretary of Labor (PN1129) — Cloture Motion Agreed to, Sep 30, 2026\n* Senate roll call 254: A bill to amend the Public Utility Regulatory Policies Act of 1978 to establish a Federal sta